 ### [Evans Ambient Occlusion](1083-evans-ambient-occlusion.md)
-Evans Ambient Occlusion approximates ambient occlusion by sampling a Signed Distance Field (SDF) along the surface normal to estimate sky visibility. It measures occlusion by comparing the distance field value at sampled points against the actual distance traveled from the surface.
+Evans Ambient Occlusion approximates ambient occlusion by sampling a Signed Distance Field (SDF) along the surface normal to estimate sky visibility. It measures occlusion by comparing the distance field value at sampled points against the actual distance traveled from the surface. It is chosen when SDFs are available and fast approximation is needed.
 
 ### [Incremental Local Ambient Occlusion](1089-incremental-local-ambient-occlusion.md)
-Incremental Local Ambient Occlusion (LAO) is a shading model for direct volume rendering that computes ambient lighting by integrating attenuated density over a local spherical neighborhood around each voxel, rather than using a constant ambient factor or global shadow rays. It solves the problem of missing local shadowing and context in volume visualization while avoiding global shadows that obscure relevant internal structures. Unlike its siblings, LAO-I computes the occlusion map incrementally, updating one ray direction per frame and storing the result in an ambient light texture using OpenGL blend operations, which allows for interactive user interaction during the computation phase.
+Incremental Local Ambient Occlusion (LAO) computes ambient lighting by integrating attenuated transfer function density over a local spherical neighborhood around each voxel, rather than using a constant ambient factor. It solves the problem of missing local shadowing in direct volume rendering while avoiding global shadows. Unlike siblings, LAO-I updates the occlusion result incrementally, processing one ray direction per frame and storing the result in an ambient light texture using OpenGL blend operations, allowing for user interaction during computation.
 
 ### [Solid Angle Early Termination for Ambient Occlusion](1146-solid-angle-early-termination-for-ambient-occlusion.md)
-Solid Angle Early Termination for Ambient Occlusion accelerates shadow ray traversal in sparse voxel structures by stopping traversal when a node subtends a solid angle below a specified threshold, effectively using a lower level-of-detail representation for distant points. It differs from [Evans Ambient Occlusion](1083-evans-ambient-occlusion.md) and [Zhukov Ambient Occlusion](2245-zhukov-ambient-occlusion.md) by relying on geometric projection thresholds rather than hemisphere sampling or precomputed angular distributions, and from [Incremental Local Ambient Occlusion](1089-incremental-local-ambient-occlusion.md) by using a static threshold rather than an adaptive accumulation scheme.
+Solid Angle Early Termination for Ambient Occlusion accelerates shadow ray traversal in sparse voxel structures by stopping traversal when a node subtends a solid angle below a specified threshold, effectively using a lower level-of-detail representation for distant points. It differs from Evans and Zhukov AO by relying on geometric projection thresholds rather than hemisphere sampling or precomputed angular distributions, and from LAO by using a static threshold rather than an adaptive accumulation scheme.
 
 ### [Zhukov Ambient Occlusion](2245-zhukov-ambient-occlusion.md)
-Zhukov Ambient Occlusion is an empirical illumination model that simulates indirect lighting by computing the geometric obscurance of a surface point, representing how open it is to the environment. Unlike radiosity, which measures secondary reflection intensity, it attenuates the constant ambient term of the Phong model based on local geometric occlusion, prioritizing computational speed and aesthetic appeal over physical accuracy. It builds on [Ambient Occlusion via Shadow Rays](878-ambient-occlusion-via-shadow-rays.md) by incorporating a cosine-weighted hemisphere integration directly into the sampling scheme.
